{
  "_comment": "Hand-maintained: where a page sends data about its visitors. 'purposes' are reported in this order; a webappanalyzer product not listed as a service falls under the first purpose whose 'categories' it has, so the specific marketing categories come before the catch-all Analytics (10 Analytics, 36 Advertising, 77 Retargeting, 71 Affiliate programs, 32 Marketing automation, 97 Customer data platform, 86 Segmentation, 74 A/B testing, 94 Referral marketing). Browser fingerprinting (83) comes before Analytics: those products identify a visitor from the device's traits, mostly against fraud, so a product that also carries Analytics is named for this. Monitoring has no category: webappanalyzer's RUM category also holds local measurement libraries (web-vitals, Boomerang) that send nothing by themselves. 'services' are session replay and monitoring vendors that webappanalyzer files under analytics, each with its 'hosts' (a domain and its subdomains; see auth-services.json for '*') taken literally from the vendor's own CSP or allowlist documentation in 'sources': a whole domain only when that documentation allows all its subdomains and the vendor's website, docs and dashboards live elsewhere, otherwise the specific telemetry hosts, and its webappanalyzer 'technologies'. A host shared with unrelated uses (c.bing.com, googleapis.com, cloudfront.net as a whole) is never listed. Traffic a site proxies through its own domain is not seen.",
